# Fundraising Admin Form Labels

When editing Partner Registry or other Fundraising admin forms:

- Do **not** rely on placeholder-only inputs. Placeholders disappear once a value is filled — admins must still see which field is which.
- Always show a **visible English label** above (or beside) the control. Match the Partner Registry pattern: `<label className="block text-xs">` + `<span className="font-medium text-gray-700">…</span>` + control with `mt-1`.
- Prefer partnership vocabulary: Fundraising Cashback Grant %, family discount display %, Official Grant Account, Partner Community Code, Change reason.
- Placeholders may still hint at **format** (e.g. BSB 6 digits, ABN `12 345 678 901`); they must not be the only name of the field.

## Partner Registry editor (`#partner-editor`)

Required visible labels (keep in sync with `scripts/verify-fundraising-admin-form-labels.ts`):

Organisation name, Organisation type, Contact name, Contact email, Contact phone, Postal / delivery address, Partner Community Code, Partnership status, Official Grant Account (section heading), Bank name, Account name, BSB, Account number, ABN (Australian Business Number), Fundraising Cashback Grant %, Family discount display %, Rate effective from, Change reason.

Search filters on the partner list may stay placeholder + `aria-label` (the control’s job is search, not a stored identity field).
